  "case": "20390-edge-notches-with-arcs-tangent-to-the-plates-side",
  "expected": {
    "body_count": 1,
    "faces": 30,
    "method": "A notch is 37 wide at the side (y 31.5 to 68.5 about y = 50) and 10 deep. Its outline from the side: an entry arc R6 about (104, 31.5) from (110, 31.5) to (105, 31.5 + sqrt(35)), a reversed arc R6 about (106, 31.5 + 2 sqrt(35)) on to (100, 31.5 + 2 sqrt(35)), the floor line x = 100, and the mirror image. Its width at y is 6 - sqrt(36 - t^2) along the first arc (t = y - 31.5 from 0 to sqrt(35)) and 4 + sqrt(36 - u^2) along the second (u from -sqrt(35) to 0); the two square-root integrals are equal and cancel, so half a notch is 6 sqrt(35) + 4 sqrt(35) + 10 (18.5 - 2 sqrt(35)) = 185 - 10 sqrt(35) and a notch 370 - 20 sqrt(35) = 251.678404 mm2. V = 220 * 220 * 15 - 4 * 6 * (370 - 20 sqrt(35)) = 717120 + 480 sqrt(35) = 719959.718296. Faces: the plate's 6 and, for each notch, its floor and five walls (four arcs and the line): 30. Tolerance: the recorded outline is the sketch solver's: its sixteen arcs keep the ideal centres (within 1e-14) with radii within 7.9e-10 of 6, and its floor lines are within 1.6e-10 of x = 100. That moves the notches' walls, 188 mm long in all and 6 deep, by at most 7.9e-10, so the volume by less than 1e-6 mm3. 1e-9 of the volume, 7.2e-4 mm3, is above that and far below a wrong cut: an entry arc's wall 0.01 mm out of place moves the volume by 0.5 mm3",
    "source": "analytic",
    "sources": [
      "tangency-labs/solidcraft#20390"
    ],
    "tolerance": {
      "rel": 1e-09
    },
    "volume_mm3": 719959.7182958878,
    "what": "a 220 x 220 x 15 plate less four notches 6 deep in its x sides, each notch's two R6 entry arcs tangent to the side: the round wall an entry arc sweeps meets the side plane a hair inside the wall (1.6e-10) and starts between the two crossings, so it touches the plane along its own end; one valid solid"
  },
